Hi Mr. White,

Because of the way the public records law is written, the Oregon Attorney G=
eneral does not have the authority to adjudicate appeals related to actions=
 taken by an elected state official, including the governor. Those matters =
may only be appealed to the circuit court.

Our office also does not have the authority to compel the governor's office=
 to take action. We can, however, provide guidance and advice on the applic=
ation of the public records law to individual requests.

I can take a look at the matter and share my thoughts with you on them. If =
the situation calls for it, I can share them with the governor's office as =
well.

To begin, please provide me with a copy of your request, including wherever=
 you made your public interest fee waiver argument, and the response from t=
he governor's office denying the request.

Thanks,

Todd

Todd Albert
Public Records Advocate
Office of the Public Records Advocate
